@@ -60,6 +60,21 @@ the host has set every enable (the register the interrupt pointer names,
 the host IPC enable, the IPC block's busy/done enables) and the
 controller's INTCTL gates it like any other source (INTSTS bit 30).
 
+The pipeline table: once the firmware runs, the three pipeline messages of
+IPC4 -- create pipeline (17), set pipeline state (19) and delete pipeline
+(18) -- are tracked by instance id and answered after the same 50 us with
+the request's type, the reply direction and a status: 0, or 5 when a
+pipeline is asked to run before it was paused (the one transition the
+model judges; every other transition is tracked as asked).  A set-state or
+delete for a pipeline that does not exist answers 9, a second create of an
+id answers 10, an instance id of 0 or past the pipeline count of the
+FW_CONFIG reply (16) answers 1, the multi-pipeline form of set-state
+answers 7: these numbers and the state a new pipeline is tracked in
+(uninitialized) are model values.  Every reply is traced decoded, e.g.
+``IPC reply type 19 (set-pipeline-state) status 0: pipeline 1: paused ->
+running``, and a request a fault drops is traced with its type:
+``IPC request dropped (set-pipeline-state) primary 0x91310004 ext 0x00000000``.
+
